WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.590
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:15.970
Last time: sorting 5, 9, 12, 21, 30

3
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:23.470
Chapter 4 · Sets

4
00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:35.120
Sort into groups. But what goes where?

5
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.400
Let's find out with a messy story!

6
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:52.800
Chintu tipped everything onto the floor!

7
00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:03.150
How would you tidy this up? Think!

8
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:14.520
Fruits → basket · Sports things → toy box

9
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:23.100
Each group belongs together. Tidy!

10
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:29.330
A group that belongs together = a SET

11
00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:38.490
Fruits · Sports things · My school bag

12
00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:51.460
Mango is a MEMBER of the set "fruits"

13
00:01:51.460 --> 00:02:01.740
Fruits: mango, banana, apple, guava

14
00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:17.680
Sports: which one doesn't belong?

15
00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:28.160
Samosa is a snack, not a sport!

16
00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:37.580
Show a set as a circle: "red things"

17
00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:47.560
Red apple, red car, red ball → inside

18
00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:57.700
Green leaf → outside. It doesn't belong.

19
00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:09.620
Two circles = a VENN DIAGRAM

20
00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:19.930
Red toy car → only A (red)

21
00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:30.250
Orange ball → only B (round)

22
00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:40.140
Red ball: red AND round. Where?

23
00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:49.220
The middle (overlap) = in BOTH sets

24
00:03:49.220 --> 00:04:01.960
Banana: not red, not round → outside

25
00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:15.320
Only A · Only B · Both · Neither

26
00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:23.150
A: things you write with · B: made of wood

27
00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:31.890
Wooden pencil → both → the middle

28
00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:47.670
Pen → A · Ruler → B · Bottle → neither

29
00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:56.690
A: yellow things · B: things you eat

30
00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:04.280
Yellow school bus. Where does it go?

31
00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:11.300
Bus → only yellow. You can't eat a bus!

32
00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:24.160
Banana → both · Roti → eat · Pencil → neither

33
00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:31.880
A: games with a ball · B: team games

34
00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:43.640
Which one goes in the middle?

35
00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:55.900
Football: ball AND team → the middle!

36
00:05:55.900 --> 00:06:05.390
Set A: 2, 4, 6, 8 · Set B: 3, 6, 9

37
00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:11.590
Which number is in BOTH sets?

38
00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:23.120
6 is in both → it goes in the middle

39
00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:27.670
Your turn: practice check

40
00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:38.050
Red things · Things you eat. An apple?

41
00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:48.290
Apple → middle: red AND you can eat it

42
00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:58.200
Red toy car → only red things

43
00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:03.600
Set = a group that belongs together

44
00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.840
Each circle is one set

45
00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:11.200
Middle = in both sets

46
00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.130
Outside = in neither set

47
00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:19.850
Chapter 4 done!

48
00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:26.650
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
